1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,050
Our AI drew this heatmap live from a phone photo of a real eye, marking exactly where it saw disease.

2
00:00:06,703 --> 00:00:16,623
I'm Aasrith Mandava from team CodePaws. At HackGT 13 we built Insight Rx: one photo of the eye becomes a treatment plan, a drug target and a referral.

3
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:24,946
Under the hood: a web app on Vercel and Neon, our AI on a real GPU through a secure Cloudflare tunnel, plus five smart services.

4
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:31,090
Every role gets its own login and sees only what it should. I'm Dr. Alex Morgan, a family doctor.

5
00:00:31,341 --> 00:00:36,581
One phone photo per eye, the patient's age and medicines, and it's off to our model on the GPU.

6
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:43,408
Our model builds on DINOv2, a vision AI that learned from millions of images, then taught to read retinas.

7
00:00:43,458 --> 00:00:51,038
After a quality check: disease needing a specialist, in both eyes. Shown a sick and a healthy eye, it picks right 98 times in 100.

8
00:00:51,392 --> 00:00:57,272
Eye vessels mirror the body, so a second model flags heart, kidney and nerve risks, each with a trust label.

9
00:00:57,626 --> 00:01:04,726
Guideline treatments are checked against current medicines, catching two eye-specific risks: semaglutide and pioglitazone.

10
00:01:05,079 --> 00:01:15,289
Then it ranks the proteins behind this disease by evidence, guidelines and drug-site certainty. Top pick: VEGF-A, which makes vessels leak, shown in 3D.

11
00:01:21,325 --> 00:01:28,655
Flip to DeepMind's AlphaFold: the drug touches 21 spots, and AlphaFold is 95 out of 100 confident about them.

12
00:01:29,007 --> 00:01:34,427
Across patients, the explorer shows drug makers where eye-detected demand meets few existing drugs.

13
00:01:34,782 --> 00:01:43,872
One click saves the patient and starts a consult: confirm, pick a specialist, sign. A SHA-256 fingerprint exposes any later change.

14
00:01:45,837 --> 00:01:49,857
The retina specialist accepts, and the next step passes to the care coordinator.

15
00:01:51,413 --> 00:01:56,773
Outside the network? Real doctors from the national NPI registry, plus a ready referral letter.

16
00:01:57,129 --> 00:02:02,409
Drug-maker questions pass a firewall: they see an age range and findings, never the patient.

17
00:02:03,771 --> 00:02:10,741
The Copilot looks up guideline passages first, then Gemini writes a cited answer, and Backboard's memory keeps it true to my habits.

18
00:02:11,882 --> 00:02:19,772
Gemini rewrites it in plain words in the patient's own language, never adding numbers or names, and ElevenLabs' multilingual voice reads it aloud.

19
00:02:23,295 --> 00:02:29,805
Every screening feeds a Tiger Data time-series database that rolls findings up daily, so trends update themselves.

20
00:02:30,161 --> 00:02:37,691
And it pays for itself: each screen read by a doctor closes a Medicare quality gap and bills code 92228.

21
00:02:38,047 --> 00:02:43,657
Every action lands in a tamper-evident audit trail, ready to stamp its fingerprint on the Solana blockchain.

22
00:02:44,015 --> 00:02:53,345
Per ten thousand patients: about 3,500 missed exams closed, $300,000 in billable reads, 2,600 people with eye disease found.

23
00:02:53,701 --> 00:03:02,571
Gemini explains, ElevenLabs speaks, Backboard remembers, Tiger Data tracks, Solana keeps records honest, and Grok voiced this video.

24
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:08,610
Insight Rx, by team CodePaws: one eye photo, the right treatment, the right doctor.

